# Source files are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# Why this file exists: with core.autocrlf=true, Windows checks these out as CRLF. Turbopack's
# server build keeps the CR inside a multi-line template literal while the browser's parser
# normalises it away, so every multi-line `className={` in a Client Component hydrated with a
# mismatch (server "\r\n\n", client "\n\n") and React discarded the server HTML for that tree.
# The committed blobs were always LF, so pinning eol here changes the checkout, not the history.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep binaries byte-for-byte.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.xlsx binary
